id: pm-wx2lr5
title: "GH-853: extension command test harness must inject the real host-bound SDK"
description: "The recommended extension activation and command-dispatch test harness omits CommandHandlerContext.sdk, so package authors cannot behavior-test commands that use context.sdk.client with host parity. Implement a default real host-bound SDK from pmRoot plus an explicit typed override seam, with public contracts, focused coverage, documentation, and installed-package acceptance."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:sdk","area:testing",authoring,extensions,gh-issue,host-parity
created_at: "2026-08-01T13:27:06.241Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T15:18:29.285Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:33.261Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:33.261Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Default test dispatch constructs a real host-bound SDK from pmRoot; A typed explicit SDK or factory override is supported without partial doubles; Public SDK tests, docs, package contracts, and isolated consumer acceptance cover the behavior"
parent: pm-usfg
severity: high
repro_steps: Use createExtensionTestHarness with a registered command that reads context.sdk.client; runCommand throws because context.sdk is undefined
expected_result: runCommand supplies the same host-bound ExtensionCommandSdk as installed dispatch and permits typed explicit injection
actual_result: runCommand builds CommandHandlerContext without sdk and exposes no injection option
affected_version: 2026.8.1
component: sdk/testing
